<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog
        xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
        xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
        http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-latest.xsd">

    <!-- V1 BASELINE (SCRUM-107, owner directive 2026-08-08).

         THE MARK_RAN GUARDS IN THIS FILE ARE LOAD-BEARING AND STAY, for the same reason as
         001's: they converge two SERVICES on one fresh database, not a migrated database
         with a fresh one. man_isr_resp, man_sbsr_resp, man_pbsr_resp and man_validation_log
         each have two creators, their owning service (MIX, MSX, MPX, MRV) and MRG here, and
         nothing serializes the ten migrations of the one dcre_man. The three ix_man_*_pick
         indexes are guarded for the same reason: they sit on tables a sibling may have
         created first. Contrast 003, 005 and 008, whose objects MRG alone creates and which
         therefore carry no guard at all in v1.

         The mandate response-leg consolidation, the exact mirror of crg's
         003-reporting ext_tx_status stack. Three per-leg pick views select the latest
         row per mandate request, then one precedence view COALESCEs PBSR > SBSR > ISR.
         There is NO writer: state is derived, which is what R-09 specified before the
         MSR projection drifted in.

         BOOTSTRAP-ORDER GUARD (same contract as crg 003-reporting and this repo's own
         001-man-spine-bootstrap): MRG is clock-launched and may run on a fresh dcre_man
         before MIX/MSX/MPX have ever executed, so each view source is pre-created here
         with a MARK_RAN tableExists guard carrying the owners' EXACT column sets and
         constraint names (mix/msx/mpx 001-man-<leg>-resp.xml, mrv 001-man-validation-log.xml).
         Whichever service runs first wins; the other side's guarded changesets MARK_RAN.
         Per-service liquibase history keeps this safe.

         Pick grain is (mndt_req_id), NOT the collections (emission_id, e2e): a pain.012
         message carries exactly ONE mandate, so there is no ISR fan-out to partition.
         That also removes the whole legacy-binding/family-fallback apparatus crg needs:
         the mandate reply correlates on the MRR-minted MndtReqId directly.

         PURE PRECEDENCE, no FSM. The "only a PBSR ACCP activates a mandate" rule, the
         expiry predicate and the override join are mandate_effective_status (005), which
         reads this view. Nothing here interprets a status code; it only picks the newest
         one per leg and ranks the legs. start_date/expiry_date are projected as the
         VARCHAR(8) CCYYMMDD the spine stores; the to_date cast belongs to 005. -->

    <changeSet id="004-bootstrap-man-isr-resp-mrg" author="dcre">
        <preConditions onFail="MARK_RAN"><not><tableExists tableName="man_isr_resp"/></not></preConditions>
        <createTable tableName="man_isr_resp">
            <column name="id" type="UUID" defaultValueComputed="gen_random_uuid()">
                <constraints primaryKey="true" nullable="false"/>
            </column>
            <column name="response_file" type="VARCHAR(128)"><constraints nullable="false"/></column>
            <column name="orgnl_msg_id" type="VARCHAR(35)"><constraints nullable="false"/></column>
            <column name="mndt_id" type="VARCHAR(35)"><constraints nullable="false"/></column>
            <column name="mndt_req_id" type="VARCHAR(35)"><constraints nullable="false"/></column>
            <column name="e2e" type="VARCHAR(35)"/>
            <column name="status" type="VARCHAR(8)"><constraints nullable="false"/></column>
            <column name="reason" type="VARCHAR(8)"/>
            <column name="version" type="BIGINT" defaultValueNumeric="0"><constraints nullable="false"/></column>
            <column name="created_at" type="TIMESTAMPTZ" defaultValueComputed="now()">
                <constraints nullable="false"/>
            </column>
            <column name="updated_at" type="TIMESTAMPTZ" defaultValueComputed="now()">
                <constraints nullable="false"/>
            </column>
        </createTable>
        <addUniqueConstraint tableName="man_isr_resp" columnNames="response_file, mndt_req_id"
                             constraintName="uq_man_isr_resp_file_mndt_req"/>
    </changeSet>

    <changeSet id="004-bootstrap-man-sbsr-resp-mrg" author="dcre">
        <preConditions onFail="MARK_RAN"><not><tableExists tableName="man_sbsr_resp"/></not></preConditions>
        <createTable tableName="man_sbsr_resp">
            <column name="id" type="UUID" defaultValueComputed="gen_random_uuid()">
                <constraints primaryKey="true" nullable="false"/>
            </column>
            <column name="response_file" type="VARCHAR(128)"><constraints nullable="false"/></column>
            <column name="orgnl_msg_id" type="VARCHAR(35)"><constraints nullable="false"/></column>
            <column name="mndt_id" type="VARCHAR(35)"><constraints nullable="false"/></column>
            <column name="mndt_req_id" type="VARCHAR(35)"><constraints nullable="false"/></column>
            <column name="e2e" type="VARCHAR(35)"/>
            <column name="status" type="VARCHAR(8)"><constraints nullable="false"/></column>
            <column name="reason" type="VARCHAR(8)"/>
            <column name="version" type="BIGINT" defaultValueNumeric="0"><constraints nullable="false"/></column>
            <column name="created_at" type="TIMESTAMPTZ" defaultValueComputed="now()">
                <constraints nullable="false"/>
            </column>
            <column name="updated_at" type="TIMESTAMPTZ" defaultValueComputed="now()">
                <constraints nullable="false"/>
            </column>
        </createTable>
        <addUniqueConstraint tableName="man_sbsr_resp" columnNames="response_file, mndt_req_id"
                             constraintName="uq_man_sbsr_resp_file_mndt_req"/>
    </changeSet>

    <changeSet id="004-bootstrap-man-pbsr-resp-mrg" author="dcre">
        <preConditions onFail="MARK_RAN"><not><tableExists tableName="man_pbsr_resp"/></not></preConditions>
        <createTable tableName="man_pbsr_resp">
            <column name="id" type="UUID" defaultValueComputed="gen_random_uuid()">
                <constraints primaryKey="true" nullable="false"/>
            </column>
            <column name="response_file" type="VARCHAR(128)"><constraints nullable="false"/></column>
            <column name="orgnl_msg_id" type="VARCHAR(35)"><constraints nullable="false"/></column>
            <column name="mndt_id" type="VARCHAR(35)"><constraints nullable="false"/></column>
            <column name="mndt_req_id" type="VARCHAR(35)"><constraints nullable="false"/></column>
            <column name="e2e" type="VARCHAR(35)"/>
            <column name="status" type="VARCHAR(8)"><constraints nullable="false"/></column>
            <column name="reason" type="VARCHAR(8)"/>
            <column name="version" type="BIGINT" defaultValueNumeric="0"><constraints nullable="false"/></column>
            <column name="created_at" type="TIMESTAMPTZ" defaultValueComputed="now()">
                <constraints nullable="false"/>
            </column>
            <column name="updated_at" type="TIMESTAMPTZ" defaultValueComputed="now()">
                <constraints nullable="false"/>
            </column>
        </createTable>
        <addUniqueConstraint tableName="man_pbsr_resp" columnNames="response_file, mndt_req_id"
                             constraintName="uq_man_pbsr_resp_file_mndt_req"/>
    </changeSet>

    <!-- Same bootstrap-order contract for the REQUEST-leg verdict sink. mnd_ext_status
         COALESCEs down to MRV's outcome, so man_validation_log is a view source exactly as
         the three reply tables are, and MRG can migrate a fresh dcre_man before MRV has ever
         run. Byte-equivalent to the owner's shape (mrv 001-man-validation-log.xml), including
         the uq_man_validation_arrival_sequence constraint name: MRV's own guarded changeset
         MARK_RANs against this and vice versa. -->
    <changeSet id="004-bootstrap-man-validation-log-mrg" author="dcre">
        <preConditions onFail="MARK_RAN"><not><tableExists tableName="man_validation_log"/></not></preConditions>
        <createTable tableName="man_validation_log">
            <column name="id" type="UUID" defaultValueComputed="gen_random_uuid()">
                <constraints primaryKey="true" nullable="false"/>
            </column>
            <column name="arrival_id" type="UUID"><constraints nullable="false"/></column>
            <column name="sequence" type="INT"><constraints nullable="false"/></column>
            <column name="outcome" type="VARCHAR(32)"><constraints nullable="false"/></column>
            <column name="detail" type="VARCHAR(256)"/>
        </createTable>
        <addUniqueConstraint tableName="man_validation_log" columnNames="arrival_id, sequence"
                             constraintName="uq_man_validation_arrival_sequence"/>
    </changeSet>

    <!-- Index-backed pick windows, created BEFORE the views that read them. Collections
         learned this the hard way (SCRUM-55, live 2026-07-16): a correlated scan of the
         ext_tx_status stack hung the AGT trigger scan for over 7 minutes on a 12,001-tx
         parent and permanently wedged it. Each index covers its pick window (partition key,
         then created_at descending), so CRDB reads the window in index order instead of
         sorting the table. The status-precedence key the pick views now lead on is an
         EXPRESSION, so it is not indexable here and is not meant to be: it only re-ranks the
         handful of rows already inside one mandate request's window, which the index has
         already narrowed. This view lands on CTV's hot path, so
         the indexes go in up front rather than after the first production stall.
         Per-index changesets with indexExists MARK_RAN guards (persistence.md file
         convention): each converges independently on any reachable DB state. -->

    <changeSet id="004-ix-man-isr-pick" author="dcre">
        <preConditions onFail="MARK_RAN">
            <not><indexExists tableName="man_isr_resp" indexName="ix_man_isr_pick"/></not>
        </preConditions>
        <createIndex tableName="man_isr_resp" indexName="ix_man_isr_pick">
            <column name="mndt_req_id"/>
            <column name="created_at" descending="true"/>
        </createIndex>
    </changeSet>

    <changeSet id="004-ix-man-sbsr-pick" author="dcre">
        <preConditions onFail="MARK_RAN">
            <not><indexExists tableName="man_sbsr_resp" indexName="ix_man_sbsr_pick"/></not>
        </preConditions>
        <createIndex tableName="man_sbsr_resp" indexName="ix_man_sbsr_pick">
            <column name="mndt_req_id"/>
            <column name="created_at" descending="true"/>
        </createIndex>
    </changeSet>

    <changeSet id="004-ix-man-pbsr-pick" author="dcre">
        <preConditions onFail="MARK_RAN">
            <not><indexExists tableName="man_pbsr_resp" indexName="ix_man_pbsr_pick"/></not>
        </preConditions>
        <createIndex tableName="man_pbsr_resp" indexName="ix_man_pbsr_pick">
            <column name="mndt_req_id"/>
            <column name="created_at" descending="true"/>
        </createIndex>
    </changeSet>

    <!-- Winning reply per mandate request per leg, one window pass (crg's prg_*_pick shape,
         minus the emission/legacy arms mandates do not have).

         STATUS PRECEDENCE LEADS THE ORDER BY, and it is load-bearing, not a heuristic.
         created_at is stamped by the DEFAULT now() when a reader INSERTs the row, and the
         three leg readers are independent concurrent Kubernetes Jobs, so that column records
         POD COMPLETION ORDER, not the order the bank sent the replies. Nothing else in the
         row is an ordering: the parser reads no wire timestamp and the reply model carries
         none. Ranking on created_at alone therefore lets a slow pod decide the truth.

         The PBSR delayed debtor-authentication path deliberately produces TWO files for one
         mandate (<stem>_PBSR.xml, usually PDNG, then <stem>-AUTH_PBSR.xml carrying the
         decision). On a live run that misordered 1 of 5 such mandates: the stale PDNG
         committed later, won the pick, and the mandate read PDNG permanently even though the
         bank had accepted it, so collections never started for a live customer. The
         response_file DESC tiebreak made a created_at tie worse rather than safe: it compares
         "_PBSR.xml" against "-AUTH_PBSR.xml", and '_' (0x5F) sorts above '-' (0x2D), so the
         STALE non-auth file won by construction.

         PDNG means "not yet decided", so a pending reply can never be the true final answer
         once a decision for the same mandate request exists. That is domain truth, it is
         order-independent, it needs no schema change and it invents no wire semantics. The
         remaining two keys are unchanged and still do their old jobs: created_at DESC among
         equally-decided rows, then response_file DESC so the pick never flips between reads.

         KNOWN LIMITATION, deliberately not solved here: a bank sending ACCP and then later
         RJCT leaves BOTH rows decided, so created_at (pod completion order) still arbitrates
         between them. The real fix is a wire-carried ordering, the pain.012 GrpHdr CreDtTm,
         which is blocked because that message profile is unattested under open archaeology
         item A-60. Guessing a format here would encode a fiction, so the gap is recorded
         instead. -->

    <changeSet id="004-mnd-isr-pick" author="dcre" runOnChange="true">
        <createView viewName="mnd_isr_pick" replaceIfExists="true"><![CDATA[
            SELECT u.mndt_req_id, u.mndt_id, u.status, u.reason
            FROM (SELECT r.mndt_req_id, r.mndt_id, r.status, r.reason,
                         row_number() OVER (PARTITION BY r.mndt_req_id
                                            ORDER BY CASE WHEN r.status = 'PDNG' THEN 0
                                                          ELSE 1 END DESC,
                                                     r.created_at DESC,
                                                     r.response_file DESC) AS pick_rank
                  FROM man_isr_resp r) AS u
            WHERE u.pick_rank = 1
        ]]></createView>
    </changeSet>

    <changeSet id="004-mnd-sbsr-pick" author="dcre" runOnChange="true">
        <createView viewName="mnd_sbsr_pick" replaceIfExists="true"><![CDATA[
            SELECT u.mndt_req_id, u.mndt_id, u.status, u.reason
            FROM (SELECT r.mndt_req_id, r.mndt_id, r.status, r.reason,
                         row_number() OVER (PARTITION BY r.mndt_req_id
                                            ORDER BY CASE WHEN r.status = 'PDNG' THEN 0
                                                          ELSE 1 END DESC,
                                                     r.created_at DESC,
                                                     r.response_file DESC) AS pick_rank
                  FROM man_sbsr_resp r) AS u
            WHERE u.pick_rank = 1
        ]]></createView>
    </changeSet>

    <changeSet id="004-mnd-pbsr-pick" author="dcre" runOnChange="true">
        <createView viewName="mnd_pbsr_pick" replaceIfExists="true"><![CDATA[
            SELECT u.mndt_req_id, u.mndt_id, u.status, u.reason
            FROM (SELECT r.mndt_req_id, r.mndt_id, r.status, r.reason,
                         row_number() OVER (PARTITION BY r.mndt_req_id
                                            ORDER BY CASE WHEN r.status = 'PDNG' THEN 0
                                                          ELSE 1 END DESC,
                                                     r.created_at DESC,
                                                     r.response_file DESC) AS pick_rank
                  FROM man_pbsr_resp r) AS u
            WHERE u.pick_rank = 1
        ]]></createView>
    </changeSet>

    <!-- The precedence view. Rows come from the MRR request spine (R-04: the spine is the
         request-leg authority), never from a reply table, so a mandate request with no
         reply yet still reads, as PDNG at stage_rank 1. The client dimension is
         mandate_request_header.client_token, exactly as crg's ext_tx_status derives client
         from tx_header.client_token. stage_rank mirrors crg's: 4 PBSR, 3 SBSR, 2 ISR,
         1 no reply.

         The COALESCE ladder bottoms out on the REQUEST-leg verdict before 'PDNG', exactly as
         collections ext_tx_status bottoms out on validation_log (CTV_PASS / the raw outcome).
         This arm is REQUIRED, not decorative: mandate_request_entry.mndt_req_id is NULLABLE,
         and MRR's B1a rule lands the later occurrence of an intra-file (mandate_ref,
         action_code) duplicate with mndt_req_id NULL + dup_in_file true, for which MRV writes
         FAIL_DUPLICATE_REF. Such an entry was never assigned a mandate request id, never
         reached Fintegrate and will NEVER receive a reply on any leg, so a bare 'PDNG' default
         made it pending FOREVER: MRG could never report it terminal, and the 1:1-live
         admission check would count it as a live twin and block a legitimate re-registration
         of that contract. stage_rank stays 1 for an MRV-only row: the verdict is the request
         leg, not a reply stage. mandate_effective_status (005) maps any non-PASS MRV outcome
         at rank 1 to RJCT, which is what makes it terminal and not live.

         action_code rides along (D5b, added 2026-07-25). It is an attribute of the
         INSTRUCTION, which is exactly this view's grain, and the per-mandate collapse
         (007 mandate_current_status) cannot be derived without it: an outcome's meaning
         depends on the action it answers, so a rejected AMEND must not be read as a
         rejected mandate. It is appended LAST on purpose: CRDB CREATE OR REPLACE VIEW
         accepts new trailing columns on a view that already has dependents, but never a
         reorder or an insertion. -->

    <changeSet id="004-mnd-ext-status" author="dcre" runOnChange="true">
        <createView viewName="mnd_ext_status" replaceIfExists="true"><![CDATA[
            SELECT h.client_token AS client,
                   e.mandate_ref,
                   e.mndt_req_id,
                   e.contract_ref,
                   e.debtor_account,
                   e.creditor_account,
                   e.max_collection_amount,
                   e.start_date,
                   e.expiry_date,
                   COALESCE(pp.status, sp.status, ip.status,
                            CASE WHEN v.outcome = 'PASS' THEN 'MRV_PASS'
                                 ELSE v.outcome END, 'PDNG')         AS raw_status,
                   COALESCE(pp.reason, sp.reason, ip.reason)         AS reason,
                   CASE WHEN pp.status IS NOT NULL THEN 4
                        WHEN sp.status IS NOT NULL THEN 3
                        WHEN ip.status IS NOT NULL THEN 2
                        ELSE 1 END                                   AS stage_rank,
                   e.action_code
            FROM mandate_request_entry e
            JOIN mandate_request_header h ON h.arrival_id = e.arrival_id
            LEFT JOIN man_validation_log v ON v.arrival_id = e.arrival_id
                                          AND v.sequence = e.sequence
            LEFT JOIN mnd_isr_pick  ip ON ip.mndt_req_id = e.mndt_req_id
            LEFT JOIN mnd_sbsr_pick sp ON sp.mndt_req_id = e.mndt_req_id
            LEFT JOIN mnd_pbsr_pick pp ON pp.mndt_req_id = e.mndt_req_id
        ]]></createView>
    </changeSet>

</databaseChangeLog>
